## Getting started

### Backend
{{if ne .Router "none"}}
```bash
go run .
```

Server listens on `:8080` — check `GET /health` once it's running.
{{else}}
No router was selected — this module has no HTTP entry point yet.
{{end}}
{{if ne .Database "none"}}
### Database

This project uses **{{.Database}}**. Copy the example env file first:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

{{if .Docker}}
### Docker

```bash
docker build -t {{.Name}} .
docker run --rm -p 8080:8080{{if ne .Database "none"}} --env-file .env{{end}} {{.Name}}
```
{{if ne .Database "none"}}
Or bring up the backend + {{.Database}} together:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```
{{end}}
{{end}}

Then start it with Docker Compose:

```bash
docker compose up -d {{.Database}}
```

Connection setup lives in `db/{{.Database}}.go`, read from the `DATABASE_URL` environment variable.
{{end}}
